read-storage-capacity-for-local-roots

Lane: cross

Unit: report-storage-capacity-for-local-roots

ChildPatch: read-storage-capacity-for-local-roots

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema

Purpose: Supply usable capacity of the app servers effective Codex home and harness filesystems to the control center without account authentication.

Requires: none

Provides: The unauthenticated storage/capacity/read RPC shares Doctors Linux usable-capacity measurement for both configured roots; aligned bounded TUI refreshes retain one app-scoped capacity sample, reject stale reads, clear failed or disconnected observations and preserve real zero.

Boundary: Own the capacity RPC, shared filesystem measurement and aligned refresh integration. Reuse native account refresh scheduling without changing account recovery or other interface modes. Do not enforce low-space admission, alter authentication, perform rendering-time filesystem IO or add private status-line items. Layout and display formatting remain with the control-center consumer.

Verification: Protocol serialization, filesystem error handling, unauthenticated configured-root integration, refresh ordering, account recovery, real-zero and unknown-state handling, app-scoped retention and disconnect clearing.

CrossGroup: control-center


